  "query_preview": "..Very dry and warm conditions continue today, with \nvery little gradient-driven wind. Warm and dry weather is expected \nagain Tuesday, but southwest winds will start to increase ahead of \nanother s/wv trough due on Wednesday. Expect mid-level moisture to \nincrease enough on Tuesday for some fair-weather CU/SC in the \nafternoon.\n\nThe trough enters the northern Great Basin by late Wednesday. This \ntrough is farther north, compared to previous solutions, so impacts \nwill be minimal. One thing to watch is enhanced southwest winds on \nWednesday, ahead of the trough. Speeds will likely reach near Wind \nAdvisory criteria and along with a continued dry boundary layer.\nLocalized near-critical Fire Weather conditions are possible.\n\nAlso for Wednesday, expect a further increase CU/SC activity, with \neven a stray shower or thunderstorm possible Wednesday afternoon. \nBehind the trough axis, expect some cooling for the rest of the \nweek, however, daytime temperatures will still be above normal.\n\nA zonal, but warm and continued dry pattern then persists into the \ncoming weekend.",
